title: The task id must be encoded as one path segment
updated: 2026-10-20T10:00:21Z
---

The task id goes into the path unencoded.

lib/WWW/Crawl4AI/Client.pm:234 builds the url with '/crawl/job/' . $task_id. The llm_request (:299) encodes the value correctly with uri_escape_utf8, the job request does not.

Failure case: the task_id "../../health" gives the uri .../crawl/job/../../health, which is not normalised, and addresses another endpoint; a ? or a # in the value splits path and query.

Decide: the task id is encoded as one UTF-8 percent encoded segment, like llm_request does.

The test that holds this down must be red against the old lib/ and fail as a failed expectation, not as a die.

Commit 38daaa2: job_status_request encodes the task id as one percent encoded UTF-8 segment (uri_escape_utf8), so it can neither address another endpoint nor split path and query. Suite: 16 files / 125 tests green (offline).

Commit 45092d6 (ersetzt 38daaa2, History neu geschrieben, Inhalt unveraendert): job_status_request kodiert die Task-ID als ein UTF-8 Segment. Suite: 17 Dateien / 135 Tests gruen (offline).
